WEBVTT

1
00:00:07.890 --> 00:00:11.430
Pizza boxes and soda cans cover the table.

2
00:00:12.110 --> 00:00:14.890
The video game team has been working hard!

3
00:00:16.150 --> 00:00:19.190
Julie, the game designer, leads the team.

4
00:00:19.490 --> 00:00:23.110
The game designer is responsible for how the game works.

5
00:00:24.370 --> 00:00:27.330
Some games are simple—pop the balloons!

6
00:00:29.450 --> 00:00:34.210
Other games tell stories with characters, like stick figures looking for a snack.

7
00:00:37.360 --> 00:00:43.680
Stories can get complex too, with huge worlds and lots of characters.

8
00:00:44.880 --> 00:00:48.580
The designer decides what can happen in the game world.

9
00:00:49.320 --> 00:00:53.380
Julie's team is making Treasure Hunter, an adventure game.

10
00:00:54.100 --> 00:00:57.620
The hero is searching around the world for ancient treasure.

11
00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:04.740
She uses a storyboard—a series of pictures—to introduce her ideas to the team.

12
00:01:05.780 --> 00:01:08.420
Today the team is planning a new level.

13
00:01:09.000 --> 00:01:10.940
The hero will go through a swamp!

14
00:01:13.400 --> 00:01:15.900
The hero needs new tools: scuba gear and insect spray.

15
00:01:17.530 --> 00:01:20.910
After the meeting everyone has a job to do.

16
00:01:22.940 --> 00:01:25.960
What will the swamp and the characters look like?

17
00:01:26.480 --> 00:01:28.320
This job is for the artists.

18
00:01:30.960 --> 00:01:33.860
They also need to draw the new tools and backgrounds.

19
00:01:35.240 --> 00:01:38.499
The artists use computers to draw everything in the game.

20
00:01:38.500 --> 00:01:45.090
The programmers write the computer code that runs the game.

21
00:01:45.510 --> 00:01:47.670
The code counts the game points.

22
00:01:48.630 --> 00:01:51.370
It also controls what the game player sees.

23
00:01:52.010 --> 00:01:54.710
The programmers make sure the game works correctly.

24
00:01:55.450 --> 00:01:58.910
When the hero jumps, he has to follow the correct path.

25
00:01:59.210 --> 00:02:01.330
Then he has to land in the right spot.

26
00:02:03.080 --> 00:02:04.980
The game needs sound too.

27
00:02:05.500 --> 00:02:09.140
The audio crew is responsible for any sounds the game makes.

28
00:02:09.740 --> 00:02:11.859
The swamp level needs new sounds.

29
00:02:11.860 --> 00:02:17.360
Splash! That's the sound for landing in the muddy water.

30
00:02:17.421 --> 00:02:22.244
Hsst! That's the sound for using bug spray.

31
00:02:22.800 --> 00:02:27.080
Sometimes the audio crew can use real sounds for the game sounds.

32
00:02:27.620 --> 00:02:30.100
The insect spray sound is easy.

33
00:02:30.600 --> 00:02:33.320
But making other sounds is more difficult.

34
00:02:34.480 --> 00:02:37.600
Why is the crew blowing bubbles with straws?

35
00:02:37.960 --> 00:02:40.340
They're making the sound for the scuba gear!

36
00:02:41.505 --> 00:02:47.816
Whew! The testers have spent hours playing the new level.

37
00:02:48.520 --> 00:02:51.500
They tell Julie what they liked and didn't like.

38
00:02:52.200 --> 00:02:55.340
They say the swamp level is a great level!

39
00:02:56.020 --> 00:02:58.240
But there are a few bugs to fix.

40
00:02:59.360 --> 00:03:01.860
Sometimes the insect spray doesn't work!

41
00:03:03.930 --> 00:03:06.690
The testers tell the programmers about the bugs.

42
00:03:07.210 --> 00:03:09.770
Their work is done for now.

43
00:03:11.340 --> 00:03:13.080
Julie's work isn't done, though.

44
00:03:14.540 --> 00:03:17.380
She already has ideas for the next level!
